<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Tracks the sibling family, and has to be RE-PINNED BY HAND to do it. It was once pinned to the
         exact 3.4.471 that FIXED the dangling-pointer bug it was written to investigate, which read as
         deliberate but is not what this tool is for any more: the README calls it a sanity check on the
         CURRENT offscreen path, and an old renderer cannot check that. Being current matters more here
         than it would elsewhere, because 7.10 was the release that fixed a hang on the OFFSCREEN submit
         path, which is the only path this tool uses.

         An earlier comment claimed it "floats with the family", which is precisely what a `X.Y.*`
         wildcard does NOT do: the star covers the PATCH, so 7.10.* could never reach 7.11, let alone
         the 7.37 the family is on today. It read as self maintaining and sat 23 minors behind.

         Every pin in src/ has that same shape and stays current only because a re-pin commit moves it
         (see "build(deps): repin onto DIR.Lib 9.0 and port the pre-layout scale to DesignScale"). This
         project sits outside src/ AND outside CPM, so those sweeps have nothing to move here, which is
         how it became the one tianwen pin left behind. It WILL drift again: the first fix of this was
         written against 7.33 and was four minors stale before it landed.

         deps.sh in the repos skill is what catches that, and the signal to look for is SdlVulkan.Renderer
         appearing TWICE in tianwen's edges, once from here and once from CPM. That pair is now marked
         `split-pin`, and a pin below what nuget.org already carries now reads BEHIND-PUBLISHED rather
         than minor-pending; before both of those it was reported in the same routine bucket as a pin
         waiting on an unpublished bump, which is why 27 minors of drift went unnoticed in plain sight. -->
    <PackageReference Include="SdlVulkan.Renderer" Version="7.37.*" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
